{title: 597 - Ye Servants of the Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #597 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 597}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G/B]Ye [C]servants of [G]the Lord,
[G/B]Each [C]in [G7/D]his [C/E]office wait,
[F]Observant of [G]His [G7/F]heavenly [G/B]Word,
[G7/D]And [C]watchful at [G]His [G7]gate.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G/B]Let [C]all your lamps [G]be bright,
[G/B]And [C]trim [G7/D]the [C/E]golden flame,
[F]Gird [Dm]up [F]your loins [G]as [G7/F]in [C/E]His sight,
[G7/D]His [C]coming thus [G]proclaim.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G/B]Watch, [C]'tis your Lord's [G]command,
[G/B]And [C]while we speak He's [F]near;
[F]Mark [Dm]the [F]first signal [G7/F]of [C/E]His hand,
[G7/D]And [C]ready all [G]appear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G/B]O [C]happy servant, [G]he,
[G/B]In [C]such [G7/D]a [C/E]posture found!
[F]He [Dm]shall [F]His Lord [G]with [G7/F]rapture [C]see,
[G7/D]And [C]be with honor [G7]crowned.
{end_of_verse}
